# BAWAAL Arena Challenge Architecture (LOCKED baseline)

High-performance stealth-black sports network centered on **asynchronous 1v1 video battles**.
Further work builds on this contract — do not regress the single video Arena feed, inline community shelf (after leading videos), slim GAME ON hub, BATTLES open callouts, 1-tap challenge camera, or post-record teardown.

## Core mechanics

- Side-by-side battle cards: **YOU / opener on the left** vs **challenger on the right** (`ArenaFeed.js` `BattleCard`).
- Open challenges: left = host benchmark (`@YOU`), right = empty RESPOND slot until athletes reply.
- Primary surface: `ArenaFeed.js` (Arena tab). Camera: `UniversalCamera.tsx`.

## Single video Arena feed (`ArenaFeed.js`)

- Main Arena is a **clutter-free cinematic video feed** — no dual-segment toggle, no floating toast/notification banners over video.
- Header: **ARENA** + top-right **GAME ON** action.
- **Inline shelf:** every **4–5** media items, inject **🔥 LIVE COMMUNITY CHALLENGES** (`CommunityChallengesShelf`) with OPEN CHALLENGES + TIPS & BREAKDOWNS (RESPOND / TEACH). Tap → `openBattlesCallout(id)` → BATTLES.
- **Cold-start rule:** list indices **0** and **1** are always video/battle media. Never inject the community shelf before at least **2** media rows have been rendered.

## GAME ON hub (scores only)

- Tap **GAME ON** opens `GameOnHub` (legacy alias: `FaceoffHub`):
  1. Live sports scores ticker (`ScoresSportsPanel` — B&W, horizontal sport filter pills).
- Do **not** reintroduce a redundant lower taxonomy sports grid or Open Callouts inside GAME ON.

## BATTLES tab — Open Callouts (source of truth)

- `BattlesScreen.js` hosts **Active Battles** and **Open Callouts**.
- Categories (`src/utils/faceoffCallout.js`): **OPEN CHALLENGES** | **TIPS & BREAKDOWNS**.
- UI panel: `src/components/OpenCalloutsPanel.js`.

## Challenge creation & camera (1-tap)

- **`+ BATTLE` FAB** / Battles **LAUNCH ARENA CHALLENGE** → **single tap** into `UniversalCamera` challenge mode.
- Keep **`RECORDING_TEARDOWN_MS = 200`** before preview/unmount.

## Re-hydration prompt (maintain)

Load project context for BAWAAL: Keep the main Arena surface as a single clutter-free cinematic video feed with ARENA + GAME ON in the header and no floating alert toasts. Indices 0–1 are always video content; every 4–5 feed items thereafter inject an inline LIVE COMMUNITY CHALLENGES shelf whose cards deep-link into BATTLES Open Callouts. GAME ON hosts live scores with horizontal sport pills only. Keep the 1-tap challenge creation route to `UniversalCamera.tsx` active, preserving the 200ms teardown delay.

